The attached image, Figure 10, displays immunofluorescence microscopy of mouse skeletal muscle injection sites 24 hours post-injection. The top row shows Nano-11 (red) with OVA, revealing uptake by Mac-2+ monocytes and MHCII+ cells, alongside recruitment of inflammatory cells including neutrophils (1A8). In contrast, the bottom row, representing soluble OVA injection, shows few inflammatory cells and no Nano-11. This demonstrates that Nano-11 induces local inflammation and is efficiently internalized by antigen-presenting cells, a key mechanism for its adjuvant effect.